cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and also
  cite the MOC program used to compute the nozzle contour and the Edenfield
  (1968) boundary layer method listed under references.
type: software
title: >-
  MOC Nozzle BLC Contour Export: physically scaled inviscid and
  boundary-layer-corrected nozzle coordinates for meshing and CNC machining
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23270234
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23270234
    description: Zenodo DOI for v1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Reddy
    given-names: MRK
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8420-6672"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheWa1kingDead/MOC_Nozzle_BLC_contour_export"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MATLAB tool that reads the wall contour computed by the method of
  characteristics program MOC_Grid_BDE (summary.out), scales it to physical
  dimensions, adds a cubic convergent section and a circular throat arc, and
  applies the Edenfield (1968) turbulent boundary layer displacement thickness
  correction with Eckert reference temperature and Sutherland viscosity. It
  writes inviscid and boundary-layer-corrected wall coordinates for mesh
  generation and for CNC machining. Axisymmetric and planar nozzles are
  supported.
keywords:
  - supersonic nozzle
  - wind tunnel nozzle
  - method of characteristics
  - boundary layer correction
  - displacement thickness
  - CNC machining
  - MATLAB
